    "turn_text": "Yep. We've been digging all day yesterday, all last night early this morning, finding some nuggets of truth for all of us today. Listen folks, it's getting crazy out there. Look at what's happening in the streets of the United States. It's not just New York, but it's everywhere across this nation. It's like it's mob rules. And there are millions of people out there that are confident. They're going to be able to change the fundamental fabric of what this nation is all about. They're going to reverse everything that made this nation and kept this nation the greatest on the face of the planet for 240 plus years. The United States of America, is it united anymore? Instead of finding commonality and building on things and discussing, having honest conversations, talking about differences, but not talking about differences to deride or diminish someone else with a different opinion than you have on any issue. That's not who the American people are supposed to be. We're supposed to be one people. Not everybody mirror images of everybody else. It's not that at all. You can be whoever you are. You don't have to think one way or two different ways or three different ways. We are guaranteed by our Constitution and by the documents, the ancillary documents that go along with it. We were told from the very beginning, this is what this nation is about. Equality, equal opportunity, equal justice under the law. A place to go when we have differences where they get serious sometimes and we have to settle them in a court of law. All of those things didn't just pop up out of the air. Men and women gave their lives for this nation. for its foundation and numerous times since it was founded to keep it what it is. We still live in the greatest nation on the planet, greatest one ever. Fundamentally, it began when a group of men and women who had lived under oppressive Northwest European family leaders that didn't really give a rip about the everyday person that lived in their country, they looked at those people just like these are an asset that we have that we can make do whatever we want them to do. Human rights, those were the things that drove our forefathers to get in those ships and head over here looking for a place where everybody could live free, not just back then, but for eternity in a nation that would always be a nation of the people governed by the people and for the people, which it still is technically today. But down where the rubber reach the road, I don't know about you, but I don't think it's so much that way anymore. Well, thanks for joining us on hump day. It's always Wednesday's or a good point in the week for me. I can look back and see what we've been through for the first couple of days and what we put together through the previous weekend. And then I can look ahead and say, Oh my gosh, Friday's coming. And that's always a good thing because weekends just give me, and I've always felt this way. Give me a chance to just breathe a little bit easier. and rebuild, start over and kind of build a new little next week. And I like that. I hope your week is going well. I hope you're not being flooded with fear and the mob rule stuff. We're going to get into a lot of things today. And we'll be moving along pretty rapidly. You will, by the way, hear from speaker Mike Johnson. What's on this show? We still have not been able to make the connection based upon his schedule for him to come back like he used to do a couple of times a month at least. But he will be back with us, but he was with Hugh Hewitt in Washington DC yesterday. And I'm gonna let you hear that. And the reason I want you to is because it gives, he does in this interview that he did with Hugh Hewitt yesterday. It gives some insight to what is in the mind and the heart of our house speaker. And I'll just give you this little tidbit up front. He's not gone over the hill. He is not turning into a leftist. There are a lot of moving parts in government. And it's impossible for any one person to be able to tell 330 million people exactly every little thing that's going on in a daily basis. It's just too much. It's overwhelming. You'll get that a bunch of other things and we're going to talk about in just a moment about our president and how he is sadly missing a presidential opportunity in which he could unite us. Joe Biden could unite us instead of fueling the division, the divisiveness, the anger and the hatred with his placated little tidbits that he throws out there that don't represent very much if anything at all fundamentally. They don't. He's just trying to flow with the flow without making a bunch of waves. And we have a whole lot more. It's gonna be a busy morning so you get ready.",
