  {
    "episode_id": 92729,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92729.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, I would be opposed to that, of course. And we heard a rumor of this before our bill was actually brought for the vote in the House. I mean, hours before. And I'll tell you what I did, Hugh, and I guess I'm breaking news here. No one knows this, but I called the White House immediately and talked with Jake Sullivan. And Tony Blinken was overseas at the moment, but I made him send me an email where he committed to me in writing. that it would not affect any of the funding that we were working on to assist Israel in this in this critical time uh... and that they would be very judicious in that he he is in indicated to me that uh... that won't happen that this is there was a mallegations of some of that many years ago it seems to have been resolved and i am very hopeful that they won't try to proceed on that if they do uh... will work will intervene",
