  {
    "episode_id": 92729,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92729.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "You know, Mr. Speaker, ignorance is a problem. I don't believe any of these students know that Israel is the original anti-colonial state. They were under the British mandate after Arthur Balfour promised a homeland for the Jews before the Holocaust. It finally came to pass in 1948. They threw out the British mandate. Yes, there are other failed colonial anti-colonial states around the world, but Israel has thrived. So I'm glad you're doing this, and I can't believe anyone would be opposed to it. Have any Democrats objected to your going to Columbia?",
