    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Oh, no, I've got it. I've got, Lawler will be there today. He, you know, he represents New York and, uh, Nicole Malliotakis and, uh, several others of the, of the, uh, New York delegation who'll be gathering there. And, and look, I've hit my hat to my friends and colleagues there. They have been very consistent. I mean, those who are in the proximity of these universities, uh, have been very active and very engaged. And look, the house has, has taken action. We, we've, we've acted to address any semitism. We, we, the house education and workforce committee, as you know, has conducted these important oversight, hearings of colleges and their leadership, some of them have gone viral online and been seen around the world, because they're failing to protect Jewish students on their campus. We passed a few pieces of legislation, the Deterrent Act, which shines light on foreign money influenced in American universities. We passed the No Immigration Benefits for Hamas Terrorist Act. Yes, it's exactly as white sound that would remove illegals who supported Hamas terrorist attacks on October 7th. But look, we passed this legislation to you. Here's the problem. It all faces a common fate. Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer controls the upper chamber in the Senate, and he is so focused on calling for new elections in Israel. he can't be bothered to protect your students here at home he's",
