    "turn_text": "One thing we can't say about our president is he is a guy who is excited. Now, when they get him all beefed up or whatever or however they get him going, remember when he gave the State of the Union message, he was on something. No question about it. I've never seen him in recent years be that energized and that angry when he gave that speech and you haven't seen that sense. You know, sometimes when you look at something and you think it's because of this, sometimes you're right. Oh well, there's still a bunch of stuff that keeps kind of creeping into the blogosphere. that is making Joe Biden appear to be even more evil than we first thought. Listen to this, this just came out. I just got this minutes ago. The Biden administration spent taxpayer dollars that were meant to fund that border wall to pay for environmental planning. Now, this is not a conspiracy. This is a fact that's according to a new report by Biden's own GAO, the government accountability office. At the request of Republican reps, Jack Bergman of Michigan, Jodi Errington of Texas, the GAO investigated whether the DHS Department of Homeland Security broke the law when it effectively blocked the use of taxpayer dollars to build a wall along the southern border. That money, that approval, that bill came from Congress. And Joe Biden just thumbed his nose at it and then decided to use it for his climate change stuff. While the GAO's final report clears the DHS of breaking the law, it confirmed that DHS used congressionally appropriated money meant for the wall to pay for environmental planning and efforts to remediate or mitigate environmental damage from past border wall construction. Republicans on the House Budget Committee, including Bergman and Errington, characterized the GAO's finding as confirmation that the Biden administration has spent taxpayer money meant to enhance Board of Security to further its environmental agenda instead. Congress approved that money for DHS to build a border barrier between fiscal year 2018 and 2021. But Biden and his appointees quickly instituted a new policy. whereby no more American taxpayer dollars would be diverted to construct a border wall upon an airing office in 2021. Cabinet secretaries, people like Alejandro Mayarchus, were ordered to work together to come up with plans for how to shift that money away from border wall construction. And they'd followed through. They went on through it in 2021. DHS released a report detailing how it would look to redirect money meant for the wall to instead pay for things like environmental planning, reviewing upcoming imminent domain actions and considering environmental remediation efforts in areas that had been the site of previous construction. The agency then changed its plans in July of 2022, applying an amendment that made environmental remediation a top priority for the agency's expenditures of the funds that were appropriated for fiscal years 2018 through 2021. Biden has made great efforts to roll back or replace a bunch of the immigration and border policies of Donald Trump. But the situation at the border has deteriorated massively since 2021, and it's way, way, way, way, way worse than it was when Trump was president. Biden doesn't want to admit it, and Democrats won't even talk about that. Anything that's going bad at the southern border, any product, fentanyl, you name it. Hundreds of billions of dollars taxpayers have been paying for Biden's border. Forgiveness, it ain't there anymore. All of that is being exposed and they're still blaming Donald Trump for every bit of it. Meanwhile, this kind of popped out over the last couple of days. Joe Biden is actually considering declaring a national climate emergency. And if he does that or any president does that, that gives himself the president powers that he can exercise without going to Congress for approval. So in the middle of facing horrible polling numbers and a lack of left-wing enthusiasm for his reelection, Biden's thinking about taking an extreme measure that shits and chills down the spines of any of us. Any of us that value our liberties, In an April 19th broadcast of the Fox Business Show, the bottom line with Dagan and Duffy, Sean Duffy co-hosts, he revealed that the Biden White House told Fox Business, it's considering defying the Constitution and declaring a climate emergency. He then turned to his guest Marco Moreno, a former Republican political aide who runs a climate change skeptic website called climatedepo.com and asked him what impact that would have. Moreno cited an NBC News report that said that if Biden declared such a climate emergency. He would have COVID-19-like emergency powers. Remember those? He put us in the darkness, kids at home, no education. The only businesses that were open were places like bars and strip clubs in California. We couldn't even go to church. If Biden does this, it would include the ability to implement the socialist Green New Deal along with up to 130 different measures with no approval from Congress. Bloomberg reports the unchecked powers could be used to curtail things like crude oil exports, suspend offshore drilling, curb greenhouse gas emissions. In other words, he could do anything he wanted to do. The Biden regime believes this would enable them to meet climate targets with the stroke of a pen like they have been doing with the stroke of his pen, despite the deleterious impact it would have on millions of our jobs. Bloomberg also said that some White House officials believe that declaring that climate emergency would energize leftist climate voters months before the election. You know what doesn't matter how wrong, how illegal, how unethical the things they plan to do, they all point to one thing. Here's the justification. This will help us in November. White House spokesman Angelo Fernandez, Hernandez, played coy when he was asked by Bloomberg about the possible climate declaration. President Biden has treated the climate crisis as an emergency since day one. We'll continue to build a clean energy future that lowers our utility bills, creates good paying, union jobs, makes our economy the envy of the world and prioritizes communities that for too long have been left behind. That's a talking point. We all know that. Meanwhile today, Californians are paying $7.29 for either. a gallon of gas or a loaf of bread. And that, my friends, is factual. That is Joe Biden's world, the reality of what he is created and what he is forcing down the throats of Americans. And he only thinks he's just getting started. He wants more power. And he looks at the short time between now And January of next year, if he loses, the new president would be inaugurated. He's not slowing down. He's slinging papers and signing papers and creating things that we don't even know about that are 100% unconstitutional. And it's nothing more than trying to make this nation be totally controlled. by Washington DC, forget about the Constitution, forget about the law. I'm Joe Biden, and I can do anything I want to do.",
