    "turn_text": "you hear on this show fairly regularly, she is an attorney, former attorney. She has a very popular show on the Internet, a talk show. And she's really good at communicating. She weighs in a lot on Donald Trump. And yesterday, she weighed into this thing that has popped up at the beginning of the Trump hush money trial, where Trump allegedly met with that magazine. I even forget the name of it, but it's one of the rags before Trump was running for president, wanted to stop some of the real negative stories that were being shopped on that market that would make Donald Trump look bad. And this was before he even announced he was considering running for president. He was just a very well-known, very public billionaire. And he didn't want a lot of this stuff to get out there. Some of it went even factual and they knew that. But they tried, and this is very normal. It happens all the time. Corporations do it. You get people, you negotiate contracts with them. They're prevented for some money that you pay them. They're saying, I will not reveal. I will not go public with any of this. And if you do, there's deep, deep trouble that you're gonna pay for doing it. It's called a non-disclosure agreement. And that's customary. It's not illegal in any way. She weighed in yesterday about this alleged get together between Trump and Cohen, who was at that time, one of Trump's lawyers, and the head of this magazine and they did come up with money to pay a couple of people that were out there saying we're going to say these in public negative things about Donald Trump. Here's Kelly, Megan Kelly.",
