  {
    "episode_id": 92729,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92729.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 136,
    "turn_text": "I don't understand it. Other than, it's very obvious, they're using anything and everything they possibly can to keep Trump from getting out on the campaign trail. And there's one thing nobody's talking about that is really important. The very obvious things are there. We know why it's going on. We know who has to be at the bottom of it. And we understand the purpose, but there's a big price being paid for all of this by a lot of people. The obvious one would be Donald Trump. He's got and is paying millions of dollars, maybe even tens of millions of dollars in legal fees for all this litigation that's being thrown at him. That's bad enough, but you know who else is paying a price for this? The American people. We're caught up in this whirlwind of, he said, she said, this is right. This is wrong. This is legal. This is not legal. You can't do this. Oh, yes, you can. You shouldn't have done this. There's no prevention in the law for me to do it over and over and over. We the people are caught up in the middle of this mess. And I don't know about you, but I am very, very uncomfortable in it. I just don't like it. Maybe it's because I'm an old guy. And maybe it's because I believe in the rule of law. And I think everything should be clean. Everything should be honest and out front. And anything we do, we should know from the get go. What it's about, what's going on, what the objectives are, all of the facts that go along with these things, so we can make good decisions. Good decisions. Boy, that's an obvious thing, a dream, a pipe dream, isn't it? But let me say this about our government. They owe that to the American people. They owe facts, not political thuggery or hackery or ideology, facts. And this administration, heck, they don't even think about factual stuff. Whenever anything comes up, they look at it with one prism. The only prism they even think about is we've got to find the way to either make this good for us politically. And if it's not good, if it's bad, we got to find a way to bury it. We can't let the American people know what we did, and we certainly can't let them know about what we're planning on doing. If they find out, they may not vote for Joe.",
