    "turn_idx": 141,
    "turn_text": "When you choose a great tasting millilite, you're choosing on taste, and that's the right choice. Not the wrong choice, because right is way better than wrong. You don't try to do the wrong thing. Wrong on, brother? Back off, and I don't even know you. If someone asks you if everything's all wrong, ask them to pull your finger. Ever read the Bill of Rongs? It was written by James Baddison and John Adams. Drawing a wrong triangle? Place this protractor at 90 degrees and sit on it. What's wrong around the corner? An 8-foot ex-con named Tiny and he wants you all it. That's wrong up your alley. Just like the drifter feeding moldy muffin stumps to his 13 hairless cats. Got a wrong hand man? I've got a cousin named Randall with clammy hands. The customer's always wrong? Well that explains the waiter's creepy grin as I ate my toast. Two wrongs do make a wrong. Am I wrong? Wrong. Said, I'll make the wrong choice, make the right choice, and choose on taste. Triple Hopsbrood Miller Lite, Taste Greatness, Miller Brewing Company, Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Great beer, great responsibility.",
